 'Validity depends on the exact imported build(), sparse polynomial arithmetic, variable ordering and primitive root. A nonzero reduction of an integral cyclotomic determinant certifies nonzero characteristic-zero determinant; rank>=4 rules out a product of two linear forms. It does not show the quadric has no points, or remove exceptional parameter/saturation branches.',
 'Fixed-size symbolic elimination may have substantial monomial growth. It is a certificate calculation with no asymptotic transform evaluator or uniform fast-cost claim.',
