('F05','api_contract','Public helper validation is weaker than the intended experiment contract','Dimension/length, nonempty-term, true-permutation, nonnegative-trial/rank and primitive-root assumptions are not uniformly enforced. Rotation reference roots are caller-supplied; generic composite n is not certified by its fourth-phase check. Covariance zip loops assume full-length outputs. finite_field_audit uses int64 with no general overflow guard.','All inspected stored callers use supported sizes, fields and shapes; no failing stored witness follows from these hypothetical extensions. Fixed p/n int64 bounds are safe.',['1','3','5','10','11','14','21','24']),
('F06','test_acceptance','Reporter success is weaker than the mathematical checks','Some audit reporters write failure statuses or only checksums without asserting final theorem outcomes; run_new omits lower_gate/minor_plane; run_all writes SCREEN_RESULTS before full completion; lineage totals are hardcoded. Stronger assertions live in discovery tests and independent comparison receipts.','Stored data inspected here actually matches its bounded expected outcomes. Presence of a file, exit zero or hardcoded pass text alone is not coverage/execution proof.',['3','4','8','9','12','13','15','18','19','20','22','23']),
